# Summary

1. A source J in the path-integral exponent makes Z a functional of J.

2. Correlators are functional derivatives of Z at J=0.

3. A free Gaussian completes the square and yields exp(i/2 JΔJ).

4. W=−i log Z generates connected correlators.

5. In QED the same steps recover S_F, D_μν, and the fermion-loop minus sign.

